<title>SINGAPORE: Major telecom groups share $1.3 bln cable deal.</title>
<headline>Major telecom groups share $1.3 bln cable deal.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Telecommunications Ltd (TELE.SI) (SingTel) said on Wednesday the following companies held the biggest stakes in a deal to build the world's longest and largest-capacity submarine cable network.</p>
<p>The total cost of the 38,000 km (23,600 mile) network, which will stretch from the South Pacific to the North Atlantic across Asia and the Middle East, is estimated to be about US$1.37 billion.</p>
<p>The deal was announced in Singapore earlier on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Reuters obtained the list from a SingTel spokesman:</p>
<p>    Group				pct    US$ million (approx)</p>
<p>    Deutsche Telekom		  4.40   60.2</p>
<p>    British Telecom		   4.38   60</p>
<p>    KDD				   4.38   60</p>
<p>    SingTel			     3.73   51</p>
<p>    Telekom Malaysia		  3.65   50</p>
<p>    Telstra of Australia	    3.55   48.6</p>
<p>    Indosat			     3.51   48</p>
<p>    France Telecom		    3.51   48</p>
<p>    VSNL of India		     3.51   48</p>
<p>    China Telecom		     2.63   36</p>
<p>A further 80 firms and telecommunications authorities hold smaller stakes in the consortium.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
